course: dictionary
lesson: 6234
title: Castle words: moat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A moat is a deep, wide ditch dug around a castle or a town. It is usually filled with water, and its job is to keep enemies out, so they cannot easily reach the walls.
explain: Use the words around moat to check its meaning. «The first castles were wooden towers on earth mounds; later castles were built of stone, with thick walls, towers, moats and drawbridges.» Moats are listed with walls and towers, so they are part of a castle's defences.
explain: The same word can mean something else in different places. «Big cats are kept behind strong mesh, thick glass or a wide ditch called a moat.» Here a moat keeps animals in. In business talk, a moat is an advantage that protects a company from its rivals, just as a castle's moat protects it from attack.
fact: A moat is a deep, wide ditch around a castle or town, usually filled with water.
fact: Moats were one way to keep enemies out, along with walls, towers and drawbridges.
fact: «Singapore Zoo uses moats and plants instead of bars.» Zoos can use moats to keep animals in.
fact: «Great apes do not swim naturally and can drown, so zoos use water moats around ape islands.»
fact: In business talk, a moat is an advantage that protects a company from rivals.
exercise: «Later castles were built of stone, with thick walls, towers, moats and drawbridges.» What is a moat? | A bridge that can be lifted up | A thick wall of stone | A tall tower where the lord watched for visitors | *A deep, wide ditch around a castle, usually filled with water
exercise: «Big cats are kept behind strong mesh, thick glass or a wide ditch called a moat.» In this sentence, what is a moat used for? | Helping the cats swim to their food | Growing flowers for the keepers | Storing the keepers' food | *Keeping the big cats in
exercise: In business talk, what might a moat mean? | *An advantage that protects a company from its rivals | A deep swimming pool at the office | A stone wall around the car park | A fast way to send letters
test: «Great apes do not swim naturally and can drown, so zoos use water moats around ape islands.» Why do zoos use water moats around ape islands? | To make the island look bigger | To help the apes learn to swim | *To keep the apes safely on their island | To give the apes a bath every day
test: What is a moat usually filled with? | *Water | Sand | Hay | Stones
exam: What does a moat do for a castle? | *Keeps enemies out | Grows food for the lord | Lights the castle at night | Keeps the castle warm in winter
